Ok, now we have ruled out that it has anything to do with
aroma.affymetrix; it is an issue with *your installation* of
affxparser that fails to read the CDF.   We will have to report this
problem/move this discussion to Bioconductor instead, but before doing
that let's work with a CDF that anyone can access.

1. Install the AffymetrixDataTestFiles Bioconductor package, i.e.

source("http://bioconductor.org/biocLite.R");
biocLite("AffymetrixDataTestFiles");

so that

library("AffymetrixDataTestFiles");

works!

2. Try the following:

library("AffymetrixDataTestFiles");
pathname <- "annotationData/chipTypes/Test3/1.XDA/Test3.CDF";
pathname <- system.file(pathname, package="AffymetrixDataTestFiles");
stopifnot(file.exists(pathname));
print(pathname);

library("affxparser");
# This Test3.CDF file should also core dump
hdr <- readCdfHeader(pathname);
str(hdr);

Does it core dump?

/Henrik

