Hi Mark,

I should have provided you with more information. Sorry about that.
No I have not checked the CDF file contents but will do that.

That's what I have ran in R:

library(aroma.affymetrix)
 verbose <- Arguments$getVerbose(-8, timestamp=TRUE)
 chipType <- "HuEx-1_0-st-v2"
 cdf <- AffymetrixCdfFile$byChipType(chipType)
 print(cdf)
 cs <- AffymetrixCelSet$byName("tissues", cdf=cdf)
bc <- RmaBackgroundCorrection(cs)
csBC <- process(bc,verbose=verbose)
qn <- QuantileNormalization(csBC, typesToUpdate="pm")
csN <- process(qn, verbose=verbose)
plmTr <- ExonRmaPlm(csN, mergeGroups=TRUE)
fit(plmTr, verbose=verbose)
qamTr <- QualityAssessmentModel(plmTr)
 plotNuse(qamTr)

 plotRle(qamTr)

 cesTr <- getChipEffectSet(plmTr)
trFit <- extractDataFrame(cesTr, units=NULL, addNames=TRUE)
write.csv(cbind(trFit), file="trFit.csv")

I have tried the previous command on a different CDF file from
affymterix and they worked fine.

Another note: I have used the same custom CDF in apt power tools (from
affymetrix) and have gotten zero results as well.

Would you like more information?>

Thanks for your help
Zaid

